From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pw4-port <pw4-port@localhost>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 14:52:51 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] PW4 Android: the Wi-Fi SDIO host is non-removable

Each system suspend attempt ends in a card detect (PM_POST_SUSPEND). It
could find the BCM4343 asleep and remove the card, and bcmdhd's removal
then hit BUG() in sdio_claim_host(): a panic when Android went to sleep
with USB connected. Stock never suspends with Wi-Fi up. wifi_card_detect()
re-arms the one scan a non-removable host gets.
---
 drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-esdhc-imx.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-esdhc-imx.c b/drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-esdhc-imx.c
index d8c53e39..a2f83db5 100644
--- a/drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-esdhc-imx.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-esdhc-imx.c
@@ -166,6 +166,8 @@ void wifi_card_detect(bool on)
 {
 	WARN_ON(!wifi_mmc_host);
 	if (on) {
+		/* non-removable (below): scan again each time the chip is powered */
+		wifi_mmc_host->rescan_entered = 0;
 		mmc_detect_change(wifi_mmc_host, 0);
 	} else {
 		if (wifi_mmc_host->card)
@@ -1147,6 +1149,15 @@ sdhci_esdhc_imx_probe_dt(struct platform_device *pdev,
 	if (of_get_property(np, "wifi-host", NULL)) {
 		wifi_mmc_host = host->mmc;
 		host->quirks2 |= SDHCI_QUIRK2_SDIO_IRQ_THREAD;
+		/*
+		 * PW4 Android: the Wi-Fi chip is soldered on and powered by its
+		 * own driver (wifi_card_detect()). Without this, every system
+		 * suspend attempt ends in a card detect (PM_POST_SUSPEND) that can
+		 * find the chip asleep, remove the card, and bcmdhd's removal
+		 * then hits BUG() in sdio_claim_host(). Stock never suspends with
+		 * Wi-Fi up; Android does.
+		 */
+		host->mmc->caps |= MMC_CAP_NONREMOVABLE;
 		dev_info(mmc_dev(host->mmc), "assigned as wifi host\n");
 	}
 
-- 
